	(text "through-hole-usb-v1: one copper layer, through-hole parts only, in its own box. A cable joins J3 to the display's\n8-way case socket (3.3V, SDA, SCL, each paired with a ground). The display runs from its own USB-C socket."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00f15780-0a28-52e3-a2ea-b9cef3bedd4e")
	)
	(text "Grounds: a USB supply needn't share the car's ground, so J2 pin 3 is a dedicated return wire to the tank bond stud.\nIt carries the sender current back to the board. Without it no current flows and the tank floats up to 3.3 V,\nso the gauge shows GROUND FAULT, never a reading. J2 pin 4 takes the screen or a second return."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "461190f1-0aa0-50c0-a62b-e1140fff03e6")
	)
	(text "Harness faults (a wire at 14.4 V): R3/R5 limit clamp current to about 10 mA each into +3V3;\nD1-D4 hold the taps inside GND..3.3 V; D5 limits transients on the signal wire and does not conduct at 14.4 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89699f86-266e-58f6-80fd-a91571b32bb1")
	)
	(text "Ratiometric, differential measurement (hardware/WIRING.md):\nVp = A0 - A3 across R1 (Rp), Vs = A3 - A1 across the sender, Rs = Rp x Vs / Vp.\nLayout rules: R2 joins R1 pin 1 by its own track (Kelvin); nothing in series between R1 and J2 pin 1;\nR7 (break-detect bias) stays on the harness side of R5. C1-C3 return to GND; the module ties A- to GND itself."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dab437bb-cf1a-54f6-b0fd-50665211c921")
	)
